Chapter: SamplerGraph

 k-diffusion's sample_euler (k_diffusion/sampling.py) at s_churn 0:
 x + (sigma' - sigma) (x - D) / sigma, as one combination of x and D.

 We say:

Section: Euler

  SamplerOps = record {
    lincomb : (Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Real, Real, Real, Integer -> Integer),
    free : (Integer -> Boolean)
  }

  euler-loop-with : SamplerOps, (Integer, Real -> Integer), Integer, List Real, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  euler-loop-with (ops) (den) (x) (sig) (i) (n) (bad) =
    if i >= list-length sig - 1 then bad
    else euler-loop-with ops den x sig (i + 1) n (bad + euler-step-with ops den x sig i n)

 Step i alone, x updated in place; 1 when it was refused, else 0.

  euler-step-with : SamplerOps, (Integer, Real -> Integer), Integer, List Real, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  euler-step-with (ops) (den) (x) (sig) (i) (n) =
    let s = list-at sig i
    in let dt = list-at sig (i + 1) - s
    in let d = den x s
    in let r = if d == 0 then 0 - 1 else ops.lincomb x d d x (1.0 + dt / s) (0.0 - dt / s) 0.0 n
    in let f = if d == 0 then True else ops.free d
    in if r < 0 then 1 else 0

  sample-euler-with : SamplerOps, (Integer, Real -> Integer), Integer, List Real, Integer -> Integer
  sample-euler-with (ops) (den) (x) (sigmas) (n) = euler-loop-with ops den x sigmas 0 n 0
